[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pylint-dev/pylint/issues/comments/411659929","html_url":"https://github.com/pylint-dev/pylint/issues/2313#issuecomment-411659929","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pylint-dev/pylint/issues/2313","id":411659929,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQxMTY1OTkyOQ==","user":{"login":"PCManticore","id":448166,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0ODE2Ng==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/448166?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PCManticore","html_url":"https://github.com/PCManticore","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PCManticore/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PCManticore/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PCManticore/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PCManticore/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PCManticore/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PCManticore/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PCManticore/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PCManticore/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PCManticore/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2018-08-09T07:10:46Z","updated_at":"2018-08-09T07:10:46Z","body":"Hi, thanks for creating an issue!\r\n\r\nThis was a weird one to debug as from a quick look it seemed that `pylint` should have imported your package correctly, since it doesn't use any potential problematic features (namespace packages and friends).\r\n\r\nFor context, pylint 2.0 uses `typed_ast` for getting access to type comments. When trying to parse the `identifiers.py` file, `typed_ast` suddenly fails with `misplaced type annotation (<unknown>, line 105)`. Not sure why as that type comment seem alright to me, so it might be a `typed_ast` bug. This exception gets transformed to an `AstroidSyntaxError` exception, which is expected. Where things get funky is later on in `pylint` where we catch `AstroidBuildingException` when we cannot import a module (https://github.com/PyCQA/pylint/blob/3a8635a9ef85759f96bfefd8edcd70e223fd12bb/pylint/checkers/imports.py#L654). This means it silently catches `AstroidSyntaxError` as well, which is inheriting from `AstroidBuildingException`. This behaviour results in `pylint` swallowing the original cause of your problem, considering that `aws_encryption_sdk` cannot be imported and most likely does not exist, resulting in the behaviour you are noticing.\r\n\r\nWe should definitely catch just the relevant exceptions here rather than catching everything with `AstroidBuildingException`. Also it's probably worth asking the `typed_ast` folks why that type comment is not proper, and most likely if you remove it, `pylint` will be able to import your module again.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pylint-dev/pylint/issues/comments/411659929/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"PCManticore","id":448166,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0ODE2Ng==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/448166?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PCManticore","html_url":"https://github.com/PCManticore","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PCManticore/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PCManticore/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PCManticore/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PCManticore/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PCManticore/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PCManticore/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PCManticore/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PCManticore/events{/privacy}","recei